.TH XD\-COMPOSITOR 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-compositor \- the XeonDesktop Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-compositor
.OP \-\-style style
.OP \-\-scheme file
.OP \-\-scale n
.OP \-\-terminal command
.OP \-\-shell path
.OP \-\-no\-shell
.OP \-\-allow\-virtual\-input
.OP \-s command
.OP \-d
.YS
.SY xd\-compositor
.B \-\-help
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-compositor
is the window manager and display server of XeonDesktop, a desktop in the
style of Windows 2000, XP and 7.
It is a wlroots compositor that draws the window frames of the chosen
visual style and runs X11 programs through Xwayland when it is installed.
.PP
It runs from a text console (through logind or seatd) or nested in another
X11 or Wayland session, where it opens a window.
Display managers start it through
.BR xeondesktop\-session (1).
.PP
At start-up it starts
.BR xd\-shell (1)
(the taskbar, Start menu and desktop) and restarts it if it crashes, and
starts the polkit agent
.BR xd\-polkit (1).
In a session on a seat it gives the session's display to systemd's user
manager and D-Bus, then starts
.I xeondesktop\-session.target
(which binds
.IR graphical\-session.target ,
so autostart entries run).
.PP
On a GPU it hands over to
.BR xd\-compositor\-fx (1),
the same compositor built with SceneFX, which blurs what is behind Aero's
glass and draws window shadows.
When every GPU is a virtual machine's (VirtualBox, VMware, virtio, QXL) it
draws in software instead, which is faster there; Aero is then opaque, as
Windows 7 Basic.
.PP
The appearance comes from
.IR desktop.ini ,
which Display Properties
.RB ( xd\-desk (1))
writes; the compositor follows changes to the file at once.
It also generates a GTK 3 theme matching the style, so GTK programs look
the same, and gives Qt programs Qt's GTK platform theme with a matching
palette unless the user set up Qt theming of their own.
.PP
It starts the input method framework chosen in Keyboard Properties
.RB ( xd\-keyboard (1),
.B [Keyboard] InputMethod
in
.IR desktop.ini ):
.BR fcitx5 ,
or IBus with
.BR "ibus start \-\-type wayland" ,
restarted if it crashes and switched when the setting changes.
Programs reach it through the compositor: Wayland programs with
text-input-v3, which the compositor relays to the input method's
input-method-v2, with its candidate window at the text cursor.
Only the input method is offered input-method-v2 and the virtual keyboard
it passes unused keys back with: a program the compositor started for it,
or an installed framework's own program
.RB ( fcitx5 ,
.BR ibus\-daemon ,
.BR ibus\-wayland ).
While the screen is locked, keys never go to the input method.
.PP
Each monitor's gamma ramp carries its calibration (the vcgt curves of the
ICC profile Color Management,
.BR xd\-color (1),
made its default; read with Little CMS) and the night light
.RB ( [NightLight] ),
changing over half an hour around sunset and sunrise or the set hours.
A program that sets the gamma itself through wlr-gamma-control
(gammastep, wlsunset) takes over while it runs.
The ramp is loaded by the display hardware, so it costs no drawing, but
nested and headless outputs have none.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-style " style"
The visual style:
.BR classic " (Windows 2000), " luna " (XP), " whistler
(Watercolor) or
.B aero
(Windows 7).
Without it the style comes from
.IR desktop.ini ,
and the default is
.BR classic .
A style given here overrides the file until the file next changes.
.TP
.BI \-\-scheme " file"
A colour scheme
.RI ( .ini
file, as in
.IR /usr/share/xeondesktop/schemes )
instead of the one in
.IR desktop.ini .
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " n"
Scale every output by
.I n
(0.5 to 4) instead of each output's own scale.
.TP
.BI \-\-terminal " command"
The terminal Ctrl+Alt+T opens (default
.BR alacritty ).
.TP
.BI \-\-shell " path"
The shell program to start instead of
.BR xd\-shell .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shell
Start no shell.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-virtual\-input
Let clients create virtual pointers and keyboards, for automated UI tests
(without it, only the input method may create a virtual keyboard).
Never use it for a real session: any program could then type and click as
you.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-startup " \fIcommand\fR"
Run
.I command
with
.B /bin/sh \-c
once the compositor is up.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Verbose logging.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Win ", " Ctrl+Esc
The Start menu.
.TP
.BR Alt+Tab ", " Alt+Shift+Tab
Switch windows; releasing Alt chooses.
.TP
.B Alt+F4
Close the window.
.TP
.B Alt+Space
The window menu.
.TP
.BR Win+Up ", " Win+Down
Maximize; restore or minimize.
.TP
.BR Win+Left ", " Win+Right
Aero Snap to half the screen, then to the next monitor (Aero).
.TP
.B Win+Shift+Up
As tall as the screen (Aero).
.TP
.BR Win+Shift+Left ", " Win+Shift+Right
Move the window to the next monitor (Aero).
.TP
.B Win+Space
Aero Peek at the desktop (Aero).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+T
A terminal
.RB ( \-\-terminal ).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+Delete
Windows Security
.RB ( xd\-security (1))
in the Classic style, Task Manager
.RB ( xd\-taskmgr (1))
in the others.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Esc
Task Manager.
.TP
.B Win+L
Lock Computer
.RB ( xd\-lock (1)).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+Backspace
Quit the compositor.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XD_VM_GPU
Set to use the GPU even when every GPU is a virtual machine's.
.TP
.B XD_HARDWARE_CURSORS
Set to try the hardware cursor where the software cursor would be used (on
virtual machines' GPUs, whose hardware cursor is often invisible).
.TP
.B WLR_RENDERER
wlroots' renderer.
Any value but
.B gles2
keeps the compositor from handing over to
.BR xd\-compositor\-fx ;
.B pixman
draws in software.
.TP
.B XD_NO_FX
Set to keep the compositor from handing over to
.BR xd\-compositor\-fx .
.TP
.B XD_ICON_THEME
The icon theme used while Display Properties leaves Icons at Default
(default
.BR breeze ,
falling back to Adwaita and hicolor).
.TP
.B XD_DATA_DIR
An absolute path to use instead of the installed data directory
.RI ( schemes ,
.IR maps ).
.TP
.B XD_SOUND_TRACE
A file to write the sounds that would play to, one per line, instead of
playing them (for tests).
.TP
.B XD_GAMMA_TRACE
A file to log every gamma ramp decided to, one per line, with what white
becomes, whether or not the output can show it (for tests).
.TP
.B XD_ACCESS_RESET_SECONDS
Accessibility Options' automatic reset after this many seconds instead of
the configured minutes (for tests).
.TP
.B XD_IME_COMMAND
A program to start as the input method instead of the chosen framework's
(for tests, with
.BR xd\-test\-ime ).
.PP
The compositor sets
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY ,
.B DISPLAY
(Xwayland),
.BR XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=XeonDesktop ,
.BR GTK_THEME ,
.BR XEONDESKTOP_PID " and"
.B XEONDESKTOP_NESTED
(0 in a session on a seat, 1 when nested or headless) for the programs it
starts.
With an input method chosen it also sets
.B XMODIFIERS
.RB ( @im=fcitx " or " @im=ibus ,
for X11 programs' XIM),
.B QT_IM_MODULE
(Qt 5, and Qt 6 before 6.8.2, which can't use text-input-v3) and
.B QT_IM_MODULES
.RB ( wayland;fcitx " or " wayland;ibus ),
unless the user set them; never
.BR GTK_IM_MODULE ,
as GTK uses text-input-v3 (Fcitx 5's guidance for wlroots compositors).
In a nested session Shut Down and the other power actions are only
printed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/desktop.ini
The desktop's settings: appearance, keyboard, mouse, accessibility and
more (default
.IR ~/.config/xeondesktop/desktop.ini ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/monitors.ini
Each monitor's resolution, refresh rate, scale, orientation and position.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/themes/XeonDesktop
The generated GTK 3 theme.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/xeondesktop
The PAM service Lock Computer checks passwords with.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xeondesktop\-session (1),
.BR xd\-compositor\-fx (1),
.BR xd\-shell (1),
.BR xd\-desk (1),
.BR xd\-color (1),
.BR xd\-lock (1)
